<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Pratiharas of Mandavyapura</h1><p class="st-meta">550 CE – 880 CE (approx.) · capital Mandavyapura</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An early Pratihara family of Marwar in Rajasthan, ruling from Mandore and known from the inscriptions of its later kings.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>According to inscriptions set up by its kings Bauka in 837 and Kakkuka in 861, the dynasty was founded by Harichandra, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmins">Brahmin</a> who had one Brahmin and one <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kshatriya">Kshatriya</a> wife; the sons of the latter founded the ruling line. They established themselves at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandore">Mandavyapura</a>, modern Mandore near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jodhpur">Jodhpur</a>, in the 6th century.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The family ruled a small kingdom in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/jodhpur-state">Marwar</a>, at first independently and later as feudatories of the more powerful <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/gurjara-pratihara">Gurjara-Pratihara</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannauj">Kannauj</a>. Kakkuka's Ghatiyala inscriptions describe him founding markets and settling merchants, and praise his skill in arms and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> learning. The family's history illustrates the emergence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> clans.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandore">Mandore</a> Pratiharas disappear from the record after the late 9th century. Mandore later passed to other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> clans, and around 1400 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rathore">Rathores</a> made it their capital before founding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jodhpur">Jodhpur</a> in 1459.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 550 CE – 880 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">South Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:70.65%;width:6.57%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>550 CE – 880 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mandavyapura</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Harichandra, Bauka, Kakkuka</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Sanskrit</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Pratiharas of Mandore, Mandore Pratiharas</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=715&amp;focus=pratiharas-of-mandavyapura" aria-label="Pratiharas of Mandavyapura on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6761 1331 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Pratiharas of Mandavyapura lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7103 1442h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7081 1587h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M7081 1587h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day India. <a href="/atlas?year=715&amp;focus=pratiharas-of-mandavyapura">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

